["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iswc", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Musical Work Code (ISWC)](https://www.iswc.org/iswc) is an 11-character unique identifier standardized by [ISO 15707](https://www.iso.org/standard/83125.html) for musical works (compositions) as distinct from specific recordings. While the \"ISWC\" label and grouping separators (dots and hyphens) are used for human readability, they shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `T0017812031`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/assistiveAutomation", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityDisclosureReport", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Vulnerability Disclosure Report (VDR) which provides the software supplier's analysis and findings describing the impact (or lack of impact) that reported vulnerabilities have on packages or products in the supplier's SBOM as defined in [NIST SP 800-161 Cybersecurity Supply Chain Risk Management Practices for Systems and Organizations](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/161/r1/final).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
